regcf.l4:143:8-84:
  I found a problem while checking the assumption of `no Regulation Crowdfunding figure exists before commencement on 2016-05-16`:
    ASSUME is an older way of introducing a name, and it is being retired.
    Nothing is broken: the file still checks, runs and exports as before.
    This one leaves
    
      `no Regulation Crowdfunding figure exists before commencement on 2016-05-16`
    
    open for somebody outside the file to supply. Say that
    with a GIVEN indented under the heading of the section whose rules
    read it (add a § heading if the file has none):
    
      § <heading>
          GIVEN `no Regulation Crowdfunding figure exists before commencement on 2016-05-16` IS A NUMBER
    
    (If this ASSUME instead marked a case the rules cannot answer, that is
    REFUSE "<the reason>" -- see doc/reference/control-flow/REFUSE.md.)
    
    The manual explains the move: doc/reference/types/ASSUME.md.
regcf.l4:494:8-83:
  I found a problem while checking the assumption of `the COVID-19 temporary rules, Rule 201(z) and (bb), are not modelled here`:
    ASSUME is an older way of introducing a name, and it is being retired.
    Nothing is broken: the file still checks, runs and exports as before.
    This one leaves
    
      `the COVID-19 temporary rules, Rule 201(z) and (bb), are not modelled here`
    
    open for somebody outside the file to supply. Say that
    with a GIVEN indented under the heading of the section whose rules
    read it (add a § heading if the file has none):
    
      § <heading>
          GIVEN `the COVID-19 temporary rules, Rule 201(z) and (bb), are not modelled here` IS A FinancialStatementRequirement
    
    (If this ASSUME instead marked a case the rules cannot answer, that is
    REFUSE "<the reason>" -- see doc/reference/control-flow/REFUSE.md.)
    
    The manual explains the move: doc/reference/types/ASSUME.md.
